# Object local names after 'await' (S0412, 3.11): reads before the await and in the awaited statement are fresh;
# branches (if-let else included), loop back-edges, continue/break paths and switches without default carry the
# state, 'while (true)' ends only by break; assignment, declarations, 'if (let)' and loop variables refresh it;
# the left path is read after the right value; '?? return' and 'try await' are covered; value types, containers
# and assets are unaffected; a stale read has type 'T?' (S0401 when passed as 'T').
